@node Introduction to Orthogonal Polynomials, Definitions for Orthogonal Polynomials, Top, Top
@section Introduction to Orthogonal Polynomials

This package provides functions for evaluating and working with classical orthogonal polynomials, the
Bessel polynomials, and some related such functions.

The primary mathematical reference for these functions is the @i{Digital Library of Mathematical Functions} (DLMF). 
The secondary reference is Abramowitz and Stegun's @i{Handbook of Mathematical Functions}.

The package supports the following classical orthogonal polynomials from Chapter 18 of the DLMF:
@itemize @bullet
@item Jacobi polynomials (@code{jacobi_p})
@item Ultraspherical (Gegenbauer) polynomials (@code{ultraspherical})
@item Chebyshev polynomials of the first kind (@code{chebyshev_t})
@item Chebyshev polynomials of the second kind (@code{chebyshev_u})
@item Legendre polynomials (@code{legendre_p})
@item Laguerre polynomials (@code{laguerre})
@item Hermite polynomials (@code{hermite})
@end itemize

Notes:
@itemize @bullet

@item Each of these polynomials are implemented as *simplifying* functions. The known simplifications 
include the facts listed in Table 18.6.1 of the DLMF. 

@item Even when an extension to negative degree is known, these functions do not extend to negative degrees.

@item For an explicit nonnegative degree, each of these functions automatically return an explicit polynomial.

@item For an explicit nonnegative degree and all other arguments numeric (either real or a complex number in
rectangular form), these functions return


@end itemize

Additionally, the package supports the spherical Bessel fuctions (DLMF, Chapter 10). These functions are

@itemize @bullet
@item Spherical Bessel functions of the first kind (@code{spherical_bessel_j})
@item Spherical Bessel functions of the second kind (@code{spherical_bessel_y})
@item Spherical Hankel functions of the first kind (@code{spherical_hankel1})
@item Spherical Hankel functions of the second kind (@code{spherical_hankel2})

Finally, the package supports the following related functions:
@itemize @bullet
@item Associated Legendre functions of the first kind (@code{assoc_legendre_p})
@item Associated Legendre functions of the second kind (@code{assoc_legendre_q})
@item Generalized Laguerre polynomials (@code{gen_laguerre})
@item Legendre functions of the second kind (@code{legendre_q})
@item Spherical harmonic functions (DLMF Chapter 14) (@code{spherical_harmonic})
@end itemize

For all supported functions with explicit integer orders, all supported functions carries out numeric evaluation for all rational, float, and 
bigfloat inputs for either real or complex and returns the result in rectangular form. Numeric evaluation follows 
Maxima’s standard contagion rules. The Hermite polynomials provide a representative example:

Examples:
@example
(%i1) hermite(5,1/2 + %i/4);
                                 121 %i   861
(%o1)                            ────── + ───
                                   32     16
(%i2) hermite(5,1/2 + %i/4.0);
(%o2)                        3.78125 %i + 53.8125
(%i3) hermite(5,1/2 + %i/4.0b0);
(%o3)                      3.78125b0 %i + 5.38125b1
(%i4) hermite(5,0.5 + %i/4);
(%o4)                        3.78125 %i + 53.8125
(%i5) hermite(5,0.5b0 + %i/4);
(%o5)                      3.78125b0 %i + 5.38125b1

@end
For explicit integer orders and a symbolic main variable, the result is an polynomial.

@node Definitions for Orthogonal Polynomials, , Introduction to Orthogonal Polynomials, Top
@section Definitions for Orthogonal Polynomials

@anchor{assoc_legendre_p}
@deffn {Function} assoc_legendre_p (@var{n}, @var{m}, @var{x})

Returns the associated Legendre function of the first kind $P_n^m(x)$. 
For a fixed integer $m \ge 0$, they can be generated starting from:
$$P_m^m(x) = (-1)^m (2m-1)!! (1-x^2)^{m/2}$$
$$P_{m+1}^m(x) = x(2m+1)P_m^m(x)$$

And advanced using the stable degree recurrence relation for $n \ge m+1$:
$$(n-m+1) P_{n+1}^m(x) = (2n+1)x P_n^m(x) - (n+m) P_{n-1}^m(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{assoc_legendre_q}
@deffn {Function} assoc_legendre_q (@var{n}, @var{m}, @var{x})

Returns the associated Legendre function of the second kind $Q_n^m(x)$.
They obey the same degree recurrence relation as $P_n^m(x)$:
$$(n-m+1) Q_{n+1}^m(x) = (2n+1)x Q_n^m(x) - (n+m) Q_{n-1}^m(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{chebyshev_t}
@deffn {Function} chebyshev_t (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Chebyshev polynomial of the first kind $T_n(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}.
Defined recursively by:
$$T_0(x) = 1$$
$$T_1(x) = x$$
$$T_n(x) = 2x T_{n-1}(x) - T_{n-2}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 2$$

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{chebyshev_u}
@deffn {Function} chebyshev_u (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Chebyshev polynomial of the second kind $U_n(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}.
Defined recursively by:
$$U_0(x) = 1$$
$$U_1(x) = 2x$$
$$U_n(x) = 2x U_{n-1}(x) - U_{n-2}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 2$$

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{gen_laguerre}
@deffn {Function} gen_laguerre (@var{n}, @var{a}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order generalized (or associated) Laguerre polynomial $L_n^{(a)}(x)$.
Defined recursively by:
$$L_0^{(a)}(x) = 1$$
$$L_1^{(a)}(x) = 1 + a - x$$
$$(n+1) L_{n+1}^{(a)}(x) = (2n + 1 + a - x) L_n^{(a)}(x) - (n + a) L_{n-1}^{(a)}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 1$$

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{hermite}
@deffn {Function} hermite (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order physicist's Hermite polynomial $H_n(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}. 
The parameter @var{n} must be a non-negative integer.

The Hermite polynomials are defined recursively by:
$$H_0(x) = 1$$
$$H_1(x) = 2x$$
$$H_n(x) = 2x H_{n-1}(x) - 2(n-1) H_{n-2}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 2$$

Alternatively, they can be expressed using Rodrigues' formula:
$$H_n(x) = (-1)^n e^{x^2} \frac{d^n}{dx^n} e^{-x^2}$$

Examples:
@example
(%i1) hermite(0, x);
(%o1)                           1
(%i2) hermite(1, x);
(%o2)                          2 x
(%i3) hermite(2, x);
(%o3)                        4 x^2 - 2
(%i4) hermite(3, x);
(%o4)                       8 x^3 - 12 x
(%i5) hermite(4, 2);
(%o5)                          76
@end example

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn 

@anchor{jacobi_p}
@deffn {Function} jacobi_p (@var{n}, @var{a}, @var{b}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Jacobi polynomial $P_n^{(a,b)}(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}. 
The parameter @var{n} must be a non-negative integer. The parameters @var{a} and @var{b} 
are typically real numbers greater than $-1$ to ensure integrability with respect to the weight function.

The Jacobi polynomials are defined recursively by the initial values:
$$P_0^{(a,b)}(x) = 1$$
$$P_1^{(a,b)}(x) = \frac{1}{2} \left[ (a - b) + (a + b + 2)x \right]$$

And for $n \ge 2$, by the three-term recurrence relation:
$$2n(n + a + b)(2n + a + b - 2) P_n^{(a,b)}(x) =$$
$$(2n + a + b - 1) \left[ (2n + a + b)(2n + a + b - 2)x + a^2 - b^2 \right] P_{n-1}^{(a,b)}(x) -$$
$$2(n + a - 1)(n + b - 1)(2n + a + b) P_{n-2}^{(a,b)}(x)$$

Alternatively, they can be expressed using Rodrigues' formula:
$$P_n^{(a,b)}(x) = \frac{(-1)^n}{2^n n!} (1-x)^{-a} (1+x)^{-b} \frac{d^n}{dx^n} \left[ (1-x)^{a+n} (1+x)^{b+n} \right]$$

Examples:
@example
(%i1) jacobi_p(0, a, b, x);
(%o1)                           1
(%i2) jacobi_p(1, a, b, x);
                          (b + a + 2) x   a - b
(%o2)                     ------------- + -----
                                2           2
(%i3) jacobi_p(2, a, b, x);
        (b + a + 3) (b + a + 4) x^2   (a - b) (b + a + 3) x   (a + 1) (a + 2)
(%o3)   --------------------------- + --------------------- + ---------------
                     2                          2                    2
                                                 (b + 1) (b + a + 3) x   (b + 1) (b + 2)
                                              - --------------------- + ---------------
                                                          2                    2
(%i4) jacobi_p(2, 2, 3, 1/2);
                                      53
(%o4)                                 --
                                      16
@end example

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{laguerre}
@deffn {Function} laguerre (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Laguerre polynomial $L_n(x)$. Equivalent to @code{gen_laguerre(n, 0, x)}.
Defined recursively by:
$$L_0(x) = 1$$
$$L_1(x) = 1 - x$$
$$(n+1) L_{n+1}(x) = (2n + 1 - x) L_n(x) - n L_{n-1}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 1$$

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{legendre_p}
@deffn {Function} legendre_p (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Legendre polynomial of the first kind $P_n(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}.
Defined recursively by:
$$P_0(x) = 1$$
$$P_1(x) = x$$
$$(n+1) P_{n+1}(x) = (2n+1)x P_n(x) - n P_{n-1}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 1$$

@opencatbox
@category{Orthogonal polynomials} @category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{legendre_q}
@deffn {Function} legendre_q (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the $n$-th order Legendre function of the second kind $Q_n(x)$ evaluated at @var{x}.
Defined recursively using the same recurrence relation as $P_n(x)$ but with different initial values:
$$Q_0(x) = \frac{1}{2} \ln\left(\frac{1+x}{1-x}\right)$$
$$Q_1(x) = \frac{x}{2} \ln\left(\frac{1+x}{1-x}\right) - 1$$
$$(n+1) Q_{n+1}(x) = (2n+1)x Q_n(x) - n Q_{n-1}(x) \quad \text{for } n \ge 1$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{spherical_bessel_j}
@deffn {Function} spherical_bessel_j (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the spherical Bessel function of the first kind $j_n(x)$.
Defined recursively by the initial seed evaluations:
$$j_0(x) = \frac{\sin x}{x}$$
$$j_1(x) = \frac{\sin x}{x^2} - \frac{\cos x}{x}$$

And advanced via the recurrence relation:
$$j_{n+1}(x) = \frac{2n+1}{x} j_n(x) - j_{n-1}(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{spherical_bessel_y}
@deffn {Function} spherical_bessel_y (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the spherical Bessel function of the second kind $y_n(x)$ (also denoted $n_n(x)$).
Defined recursively by:
$$y_0(x) = -\frac{\cos x}{x}$$
$$y_1(x) = -\frac{\cos x}{x^2} - \frac{\sin x}{x}$$

And advanced via the identical recurrence relation:
$$y_{n+1}(x) = \frac{2n+1}{x} y_n(x) - y_{n-1}(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{spherical_hankel1}
@deffn {Function} spherical_hankel1 (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the spherical Hankel function of the first kind $h_n^{(1)}(x) = j_n(x) + i y_n(x)$.
Defined recursively via:
$$h_0^{(1)}(x) = -i \frac{e^{ix}}{x}$$
$$h_1^{(1)}(x) = \left( -\frac{i}{x^2} - \frac{1}{x} \right) e^{ix}$$
$$h_{n+1}^{(1)}(x) = \frac{2n+1}{x} h_n^{(1)}(x) - h_{n-1}^{(1)}(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{spherical_hankel2}
@deffn {Function} spherical_hankel2 (@var{n}, @var{x})

Returns the spherical Hankel function of the second kind $h_n^{(2)}(x) = j_n(x) - i y_n(x)$.
Defined recursively via:
$$h_0^{(2)}(x) = i \frac{e^{-ix}}{x}$$
$$h_1^{(2)}(x) = \left( \frac{i}{x^2} - \frac{1}{x} \right) e^{-ix}$$
$$h_{n+1}^{(2)}(x) = \frac{2n+1}{x} h_n^{(2)}(x) - h_{n-1}^{(2)}(x)$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

@anchor{spherical_harmonic}
@deffn {Function} spherical_harmonic (@var{n}, @var{m}, @var{theta}, @var{phi})

Returns the spherical harmonic function $Y_n^m(\theta, \phi)$ of degree @var{n} and order @var{m}.
It is expressed directly in terms of the associated Legendre functions @code{assoc_legendre_p}:

$$Y_n^m(\theta, \phi) = \sqrt{\frac{2n+1}{4\pi} \frac{(n-m)!}{(n+m)!}} P_n^m(\cos \theta) e^{im\phi}$$

Where properties for negative $m$ are satisfied via the relation:
$$Y_n^{-m}(\theta, \phi) = (-1)^m \left( Y_n^m(\theta, \phi) \right)^*$$

@opencatbox
@category{Special functions}
@closecatbox
@end deffn

